  "term": "Meridia",
  "definition": "Meridia is sibutramine hydrochloride, a phenethylamine-derived drug with appetite-suppressing effects. Its active metabolites reduce reuptake of norepinephrine and serotonin, and to a lesser extent dopamine, which can increase feelings of fullness and lower calorie intake.",
